From 2c26fb74ef25ddf887d1de056a209cdf3d721ac5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrey Korshunov <razor1702@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 18:14:39 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] airoha: an7581: move the Gemtek W1700K DTS into a common dtsi

The Gemtek XR1710G is a close relative of the W1700K and shares almost
all of its device tree: flash layout and UBI volumes, MAC addresses,
Wi-Fi, Ethernet, the 10G PHYs, the reset button and the status LEDs.
Move these parts into an7581-gemtek-common.dtsi and keep only
what is specific to the W1700K in its DTS: the GPIO driven lan3/lan4
LEDs, the 10G PHY LEDs and the UARTs of the Bluetooth/Zigbee radio and
the GPS.

While at it, reference the wan_mac cell without an argument: it is a
plain cell, not a "mac-base" one with #nvmem-cell-cells, so the
trailing 0 was invalid and only worked because the nvmem core ignores
it for index 0. Also use generic node names for the Wi-Fi and the BMT
partition, and sort the status LEDs by GPIO (white 20 before red 29),
which swaps the led-2 and led-3 node names. The resulting devicetree
is otherwise unchanged.

Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Andrey Korshunov <razor1702@gmail.com>
---
